What evidence supports the involvement of clonal hematopoiesis in the pathogenesis of TFH peripheral T-cell lymphoma (TFHL)?,"The study found that 97% of TFHL patients had clonal hematopoiesis (CH) defined by at least one somatic mutation detected in myeloid clones or total bone marrow cells. Mutations in genes commonly altered in TFHL such as RHOA, TET2, DNMT3A, and IDH2 were identified in both hematopoietic progenitors and malignant lymph node biopsies, indicating that TFHL derives from clonal hematopoiesis and that the lymphoma shares a phylogenetic link with mutated myeloid progenitors.",hs9-7-e1859693.pdf,14,0,"S238 CLONAL ARCHITECTURE OF RELAPSED OR REFRACTORY ANGIOIMMUNOBLASTIC T-CELL LYMPHOMA: AN ANCILLARY STUDY OF THE ORACLE TRIAL, A LYSA STUDY Topic: Lymphoma biology and translational studies Romain Loyaux1, Nouhoum Sako1, Violaine Tran Quang1,2,3, Emmanuel Bachy4,5, Franck Morschhauser6, Guillaume Cartron7, Remy Gressin8, Nicolas Daguindau9, Steven Le Gouill10, Cyrielle Robe11,1, Elisa Boudali1,2, Marie-Helene Delfau-Larue1,3,2, Jehan Dupuis12, Laurence De Leval13,14,15 , Philippe Gaulard2,1,11 , Francois Lemonnier*1,12,2 , Ivan Sloma2,3,1,2 1Mondor Institute For Biomedical Research, Creteil, France; 2Paris-Est Creteil University, Creteil, France; 3Hematology And Immunology Department, ap- Hp - Henri Mondor University Hospital, Creteil, France; 4Hospices Civils De Lyon - Hcl, Lyon, France; 5Université Claude Bernard Lyon 1, Lyon, France; 6Service Des Maladies Du Sang, Chu De Lille, Lille, France; 7Département D’Hématologie Clinique, Hospital Center University De Montpellier, Montpellier, France; 8Hematology Department, Grenoble University Hospital, France; 9Hematologydepartment, Ch Annecy Genevois, Annecy, France; 10Hematology Department, Chu De Nantes, France; 11Pathology Department, Ap-Hp - Henri Mondor University Hospital, Creteil, France; 12Service Unité Hémopathies Lymphoïdes, Ap-Hp - Henri Mondor University Hospital, Creteil, France; 13Department Of Laboratory Medicine And Pathology, Lausanne University Hospital, Lausanne, Switzerland; 14Lausanne University, Lausanne, Switzerland; 15Institute Of Pathology, Lausanne, Switzerland Background: The lymphomagenesis of TFH peripheral T-cell lymphoma (TFHL) notably involves altered TCR signaling and epigenetic regulation in follicular T-helper lymphocytes resulting from recurrent mutations in key components of these pathways such as RHOA and TET2 , DNMT3A , or IDH2 respectively. Previous studies also identified some of these mutations in B cells or hematopoietic progenitors in TFHL patients suggesting that TFHL derives from clonal hematopoiesis. Aims: This study aims to characterize the clonal hierarchy of TFHL further and estimate the frequency of TFHL derived from clonal hematopoiesis (CH-TFHL) in an ancillary study of the randomized Phase 3 clinical trial, ORACLE (NCT03593018), evaluating the efficacy and safety of oral 5-azacitidine (CC-486) compared to single-agent",True,0,gpt-4.1-mini,OpenAI Ada-002 (CPU/Cloud),biomedical-review
