 Benigni A, Auray-Blais C. Biomarkers of Fabry disease nephropathy. Clin J Am Soc Nephrol 5: 360-364, 2010. 6.Sueoka H, Aoki M, Tsukimura T, Togawa T, Sakuraba H. Distri- butions of globotriaosylceramide i soforms, and globotriaosylsphin- gosine and its analogues in an α-galactosidase A knockout mouse, a model of Fabry disease. PLoS One 10: 0144958, 2015. 7.Rocchetti MT, Spadaccino F, Catalano V, et",False,-1,gpt-4.1-mini,OpenAI Ada-002 (CPU/Cloud),biomedical-review
"How do plasma Lyso-Gb3 levels and its analogs differ among classic Fabry men, later-onset Fabry men, Fabry women, and controls?","Plasma Lyso-Gb3 levels are highest in classic Fabry men (180±75 nmol/L), significantly elevated compared to controls (0.44±0.15 nmol/L). Later-onset Fabry men (17±9 nmol/L) and Fabry women (11±8 nmol/L) have lower levels than classic Fabry men but still significantly higher than controls. At least five Lyso-Gb3 analogs were detected in classic Fabry men, with Lyso-Gb3 (-2) present in almost all Fabry patients except some women and absent in controls.",63_2493-23.pdf,33,3,"Lyso-Gb3as the IS and the concentration was expressed in nmol/L.The concentrations of Lyso-Gb3 analogs in plasma were de-termined as the peak area ratios for stable isotope-labelledLyso-Gb3, as Lyso-Gb3 analog standards were not available.For comparison, the ratio of the peak area of plasma Lyso-Gb3 to that of IS was also determined. The theoretical masses of major urinary Gb3 isoforms, which have various fatty acids linked with Lyso-Gb3 (d18:1), were determined (although some MS peaks were consid-ered to be mixtures of two or more structural isomers). Theywere quantified by LC-MS/MS using Gb3 (C17:0) as IS,with the concentration of each urinary Gb3 isoform ex-pressed in μg/mg creatinine, and the total Gb3 content ofthe urine samples was calculated from the sum of the Gb3isoforms. The creatinine levels were measured using a com-mercially available assay kit. Statistical analyses Data are expressed as the mean±SD. Statistical analyses were performed using Student’s t-test to compare plasmaLyso-Gb3 levels in various phenotypic Fabry disease patientgroups. Values were considered statistically significant at p<0.05. Results Lyso-Gb3 and related analogs in plasma Plasma Lyso-Gb3 concentrations in Fabry patients and control subjects were determined by LC-MS/MS. The results Intern Med 63: 1531-1537, 2024 DOI: 10.2169 /internalmedicine.2493-23 1534Figure ɹ2.ɹPlasma concentrations of (a) Lyso-Gb3 and (b) related analogs in various phenotypic Fabry groups (blue columns, classic Fabry men; red columns, later-onset Fabry men; and green col-umns, Fabry women) and controls (yellow column) (they were calculated as the ratios of their peak areas to that of the IS; # data not available because the substrate levels were below the limits of detec- tion), and (c) ratio (%) of each Lyso-Gb3 analog to the total Lyso-Gb3 analogs in plasma from indi-vidual cases in the classic Fabry man group. The graph is color-coded as indicated in the Figure. The patient numbers are presented in descending order from the",True,2,gpt-4.1-mini,OpenAI Ada-002 (CPU/Cloud),biomedical-review
Which Lyso-Gb3 analog was most frequently detected and at higher levels in Fabry patients compared to controls?,"Lyso-Gb3 (-2) was detected in almost all Fabry patients except for a few Fabry women, was not detected in any controls, and showed higher levels than other Lyso-Gb3 analogs in Fabry patients.",63_2493-23.pdf,33,4,"men, although their levelswere lower than those of Lyso-Gb3 (Fig. 2a, b). Among thefive plasma Lyso-Gb3 analogs, Lyso-Gb3 (-2) was detectedin almost all Fabry patients except for a few Fabry women,but not in any of the controls (peak area ratio <0.01), and itshowed a higher level than the other Lyso-Gb3 analogs inthe Fabry patients. Furthermore, we determined the ratio (%) of each Lyso- Gb3 analog to the total Lyso-Gb3 analogs in plasma sam-ples from individual classic Fabry men, and summarized theresults in Fig. 2c. Minor differences were observed betweenthem.Gb3 isoforms and total Gb3 in urine The major Gb3 isoforms with Lyso-Gb3 (d18:1) and het- erogeneous fatty acids as components, in urine were quanti-fied by LC-MS/MS, and the results are shown in Fig. 3a.Various Gb3 (d18:1) isoforms, i ncluding Gb3 (C16:0), Gb3 (C18:0), Gb3 (C20:0), Gb3 (C22:1), Gb3 (C22:0), Gb3(C24:1), Gb3 (C24:0), and Gb3 (C24:0-OH), were detectedin urinary samples from almost all Fabry disease patientsexcept for a few Fabry women. In contrast, only traceamounts or no substrates were detected in the control sam-ples. Among the major Gb3 isoforms, high urinary excretionwas found for Gb3 (C22:0), Gb3 (C24:1), and Gb3 (C24:0)in patients with Fabry disease. The mean total urinary Gb3 level±SD was calculated to be 5.04±2.69, 0.59±0.30, 0.47±0.42, and <0.05 μg/mg cre-atinine for classic Fabry men (n=5), later-onset Fabry men(n=5), Fabry women (n=17), and control subjects (n=11), re-spectively. The mean total urinary Gb3 excretion was higherin the order of classic Fabry men, later-onset Fabry men,Fabry women, and controls. We determined the ratio (%) of each Gb3 isoform to the total Gb3 isoforms in urine from individual patients withclassic Fabry disease, and the results are summarized inFig. 3b. Minor differences were observed between them. Intern Med 63: 1531-1537, 2024 DOI: 10.2169 /internalmedicine.2493-23 1535Figure ɹ3.ɹ(a) Urinary excretion of Gb3 isoforms in various phenotypic Fabry",True,0,gpt-4.1-mini,OpenAI Ada-002 (CPU/Cloud),biomedical-review
What roles do Growth Differentiation Factor-15 (GDF-15) and galectins play in cardiac and kidney diseases according to recent studies?,"Growth Differentiation Factor-15 (GDF-15) is involved in adverse cardiac remodeling, serves as a biomarker for myocardial involvement in idiopathic inflammatory myopathy, and ameliorates liver fibrosis by reprogramming macrophages to acquire anti-inflammatory properties. It is also significant in kidney diseases. Galectins, particularly galectin-3 and galectin-9, are associated with coronary artery disease, severe heart failure, cardiac fibrosis, and early detection of various diseases. Galectin-3 predicts incident heart failure and is a potential anti-inflammatory target in asthma.",c50def1e-5cca-457a-a24a-c8ed98ebe70c.pdf,34,11,"Classical F abry Disease under Enzyme Replacement Ther apy. Kidne y Blood Pr ess Res 47:229–238. 10.1159/000521329 7. Zhu L, Li C, Liu Q, X u W, Zhou X (2019) Molecular biomark ers in car diac hyper trophy . J Cell Mol Med 23:1671–1677. 10.1111/jcmm.14129 Page 11/13␀. Wesseling M, de P oel JHC, de Jager SC (2020) A. Gr owth diff erentiation fact or 15 in adv erse car diac remodelling: fr om biomark er to causal pla yer. ESC Hear t Fail 7:1488–1501. 10.1002/ehf2.12728 9. Abulizi P et al (2017) Gr owth Diff erentiation F actor-15 De␀ciency A ugments In␀ammat ory Response and Exacerbates Septic Hear t and Renal Injur y Induced b y Lipopolysaccharide. Sci Rep 7:1037. 10.1038/s41598-017-00902-5 10. Qiu M et al (2021) The diagnostic v alue of GDF-15 for my ocar dial inv olvement in idiopathic in␀ammat ory my opathy . Rheumat ology (Oxfor d) 60:2826–2833. 10.1093/rheumat ology/k eaa721 11. Li X et al (2023) GDF15 Amelior ates Liv er Fibr osis b y Metabolic Repr ogramming of Macr ophages t o Acquir e Anti-In␀ammat ory Proper ties. Cell Mol Gastr oenter ol Hepat ol 16:711–734. 10.1016/j.jcmgh.2023.07.009 12. Delrue C, Speeckaer t R, Delanghe JR, Speeckaer t MM (2023) Gr owth diff erentiation fact or 15 (GDF- 15) in