What role do matrix metalloproteinases play in cholestasis and hepatic ischemia/reperfusion injury according to the referenced studies?,"Matrix metalloproteinases are involved in the pathological processes of cholestasis and hepatic ischemia/reperfusion injury, contributing to tissue remodeling and injury as reviewed in the referenced studies.",ijms-19-02634.pdf,70,16,"31. Fukushima, S.; Okuno, H.; Shibatani, N.; Nakahashi, Y.; Seki, T.; Okazaki, K. Effect of biliary obstruction and internal biliary drainage on hepatic cytochrome P450 isozymes in rats. World J. Gastroenterol. 2008 ,14, 2556–2560. [CrossRef] [PubMed] Int. J. Mol. Sci. 2018 ,19, 2634 12 of 13 32. Marcu, L. Characterization of type I, II, III, IV , and V collagens by time-resolved laser-induced ﬂuorescence spectroscopy. Proc. SPIE 2000 ,3917 , 93–101. [CrossRef] 33. Derosa, G.; Mafﬁoli, P . Traditional Markers in Liver Disease. In Biomarkers in Liver Disease ; Springer: Dordrecht, The Netherlands, 2017; pp. 3–22, ISBN 9400776748. 34. Croce, A.C.; de Simone, U.; Freitas, I.; Boncompagni, E.; Neri, D.; Cillo, U.; Bottiroli, G. Human liver autoﬂuorescence: An intrinsic tissue parameter discriminating normal and diseased conditions. Lasers Surg. Med. 2010 ,42, 371–378. [CrossRef] [PubMed] 35. Palladini, G.; Ferrigno, A.; Richelmi, P .; Perlini, S.; Vairetti, M. Role of matrix metalloproteinases in cholestasis and hepatic ischemia/reperfusion injury: A review. World J. Gastroenterol. 2015 ,21, 12114–12124. [CrossRef] [PubMed] 36. Palladini, G.; Ferrigno, A.; Rizzo, V .; Boncompagni, E.; Richelmi, P .; Freitas, I.; Perlini, S.; Vairetti, M. Lobe-speciﬁc heterogeneity and matrix metalloproteinase activation after ischemia/reperfusion injury in rat livers. Toxicol. Pathol. 2012 ,40, 722–730. [CrossRef] [PubMed] 37. Croce, A.C.; Ferrigno, A.; Piccolini, V .M.; Tarantola, E.; Boncompagni, E.; Bertone, V .; Milanesi, G.; Freitas, I.; Vairetti, M.; Bottiroli, G. Integrated autoﬂuorescence characterization of a mod